331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Preliminary feedback identified the need to ensure activity providers provide safe and inclusive environments for youth to avoid discrimination. This led to the development of detailed activity provider approval guidelines, and suggested eligible activities across different categories. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Further development required researching different activities available to youth, along with their associated costs. A major roadblock was identifying a target area to focus on; since an in-person visit to YSB Ottawa was a major source of inspiration for the YCCF, the team decided to focus on Ottawa service providers. This led to the development of an activity provider directory for the Ottawa region. The development of this directory showed that different activities have widely varied costs, which pushed the development of a tiered funding model & application system to support youth in accessing activities across different categories. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Additionally, partner feedback regarding funding sources and details concerning implementing the YCCF became fuel for the creation of a pilot project implementation plan. The plan aimed to cover the fine details of implementing a small pilot project, including funding strategies, partnerships, budgeting, staffing, participant experiences, outcomes, and more. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
