<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 234 0 R
/E (The YCCF supports SDG 3 by promoting mental health well-being, social connection, and healthy routines for youth experiencing housing instability. By helping these youth to access recreation, arts, sports, and skill-building activities, the fund creates opportunities for youth to belong in their community, supporting the development of support networks outside of institutional settings.  )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
375 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 234 0 R
/E (SDG 4 would be indirectly positively impacted by the YCCF by improving youth access to informal learning opportunities, including STEAM programs, workshops, leadership activities, and life-skill building programs. These opportunities can hlep youth build confidence, personal growth, and future education pathways.  )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
376 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 234 0 R
/E (The activities supported by the YCCF directly help youth in building transferable skills relevant to employment and adulthood. Volunteering, leadership programs, sports, arts, and skill-building activities help to support improvement in communication, teamwork, responsibility, confidence, and ultimately career readiness. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 234 0 R
/E (The YCCF strongly aligns with SDG 10 by reducing financial barriers of entry to community activities for youth excperiencing homelessness, housing instability, or financial hardship. The fund aims to make activities such as sports, arts, recreation, and volunteering more accessible to youth who may otherwise be excluded because of cost. Additionally, the vetting process for activity providers ensures a safe and inclusive space for all youth. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 234 0 R
/E (The YCCF supports SDG 11 by helping youth to connect within their local communities. By linking youth to Ottawa-based activity providers, community organizations, volunteering opportunities and recreational spaces, the project encourages inclusion, belonging, and participation in community life, building a strong and sustainable community from the bottom up. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
