<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Then began the sprints. Day 1 was mostly planning. Some things that got done were mapping a rough service flow and deciding on which city to focus the plan on initially. Day 2 kicked off a lot of tasks, mostly regarding researching and creating guidelines. The major things accomplished were the creation of the activity directory with costs, as well as activity provider approval guidelines and a management plan.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Day 3 was when the big projects happened. Everyone had a different major task to work on, and we all completed our tasks on time. These tasks included the implementation plan, website, flow charts, infographics, and a supplemental application. Day 4 was simply putting together all of the work.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
472 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Finally, the project was revised and tweaked one final time using the feedback from the demo presentation day. This included tightening management descriptions, clearing up roles, and adding additional sections to the risks and mitigations.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
